    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d77">

                <pb facs="0192" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg76"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 493.11/513.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Chargé MacMurray.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 20, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This Department does not appear to have authority affirmatively to sanction the
                    postponement of indemnity payments or the alteration of the schedule, but if the
                    postponement of the payment of deficiencies is unavoidable, and a majority of
                    the powers interested agree to wait until the end of the war, it is extremely
                    unlikely that any demand for immediate payment would be made by this Government
                    under present circumstances, and this Government is willing to use its good
                    offices to that end with other powers if requested. The Department trusts that
                    the deficit will not be so large as to interfere with the support of the
                    Chinghua College.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
